    "summary": "Single simply-supported 30 m precast prestressed small-box girder bridge modeled as a 2D spine beam (structure.system = simply_supported). Three girders per span combined into one equivalent beam; each 30 m span carries 6 plain laminated elastomeric bearings (two per girder end, 300×400 mm, 5×8 mm rubber layers) at both abutments, modeled with vertical and longitudinal springs.\n\nRoot cause of the failed checks: girder.A had been accepted equal to the single-girder area (1.1389 m²) instead of the combined precast section area required by MR-02 (A = A_single × n_girders = 3.4168 m²). This contradicted girder.w (88.836 kN/m = γ·A×3) and made the L3-2 total self-weight check (γ·A·L) fail. I re-proposed girder.A = 3.4168 m² with MR-02 evidence, re-ran the modal analysis, and regenerated.\n\nKey results: f1 = 3.402 Hz (vertical bending); γ = 26 kN/m³ (C40 prestressed), w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m; lane.mu = 0.2006 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2, Class II, 2 lanes, ξ = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 240 kN). Model now passes L1/L2/L3: total self-weight reactions 2×1332.5 = 2665 kN = 88.836 × 30 m; midspan self-weight moment 9994 kN·m; lane live-load max positive moment 6450 kN·m. All decisions remain accepted; no unresolved issues."
